Subject: [MAT] retain source detection indices in ByteTrack associations

Upstream commit: d1bf0191adff59bc8fcfeaa0b33d3d1642552a99
Upstream file: yolox/tracker/byte_tracker.py

This patch is intentionally kept as an audit artifact. Apply only to the locked
upstream file after verifying context. It does not change matching thresholds or
association decisions.

--- a/yolox/tracker/byte_tracker.py
+++ b/yolox/tracker/byte_tracker.py
@@
-    def __init__(self, tlwh, score):
+    def __init__(self, tlwh, score, source_detection_index=None):
@@
-        self._tlwh = np.asarray(tlwh, dtype=np.float)
+        self._tlwh = np.asarray(tlwh, dtype=np.float64)
+        self.source_detection_index = source_detection_index
@@
     def re_activate(self, new_track, frame_id, new_id=False):
+        self.source_detection_index = new_track.source_detection_index
@@
     def update(self, new_track, frame_id):
+        self.source_detection_index = new_track.source_detection_index

At each high/low score filter, carry `np.arange(N)` alongside detections and pass
the original index into STrack. The MAT wrapper returns `None` for source index on
pure Kalman predictions. This file does not claim to be an applied patch until an
integration run against the exact commit succeeds.

